OK. So what are their stategies? We can only talk about games we know
about. In my own games, the protection racket gives me a big leg up
heading into mid game.

And once again, in practice the protection racket simply isn't getting
to MineTown at XL1 never having killed anything. It's making MineTown
the first real target of the game, and getting to the altar with enough
money to get naked AC down to 1 (or maybe 0 since that extra point isn't
too very tough). This can be achieved at XL2 or higher. There's a lot of
money in the top 4 levels of the Dungeon and the Mines.

Getting back to your serial ascenders, what's the early game strategy then?
What do they do to get a leg up on the Dungeon to get to mid and late game?

By proffering the protection racket, advocates such as myself give a goal,
a mechanism to achieve that goal, and tangible results once the goal has
been achieved. Results that can assist you deep into the dungeon.

>However, it is very valuable for a new player to play the racket a few
>times to get used to running away, letting the pet fight, writing
>Elbereth, etc.  It forces you to learn a bunch of tactics you might not
>use otherwise.

There's that too. But I can't understand why you are dismissive of points
